                                "example_id": "93bdf7cb-fc3c-44f0-aed3-df1d2bf66bd3",
                                "sense_id": "8359054d-3bd4-3b59-82bd-534048d1a360",
                                "text": "17thC, Richard Baxter, The Life of Faith, 1838, The Practical Works of Richard Baxter, Volume 3, page 690,\n6. God must then be known in his three personalities; as the Father, the Word or Son, and the Spirit.\n7. And these in their three causalities; efficient, dirigent, and final."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "c09e1360-14d5-4add-8053-0d9b8ed88f52",
                                "sense_id": "8359054d-3bd4-3b59-82bd-534048d1a360",
                                "text": "17thC, Richard Baxter, Mr. Baxter's Dying Thoughts, 1838, The Practical Works of Richard Baxter, Volume 3, page 1012,\nV. I shall better know the methods and perfections of the Scripture, and all God's dirigent word and will."
                            }
                        ]
